 Pointer. The empty pointer resolves the full document; object-member and array-element tokens follow
 the standard escaping rules (`~0` for `~` and `~1` for `/`). It throws when the pointer is malformed
 or does not identify a value.
+
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an RFC 6902 JSON Patch document and returns a new JSON value.
+It supports `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, and `test`, including root and array-append
+targets. It validates operation shape and JSON Pointer syntax, ignores operation members not defined by
+the selected operation, and throws when an operation fails. Inputs are not mutated, so a failing patch
+leaves the caller's source document unchanged.
